{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-10-Nov-2022-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "−1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A shopkeeper sells his items using a faulty balance which measures 25% less. He then marks up his items 15% above the cost price. If he also gives a discount of 10%, then find his net profit percentage on 1 kg items.", "options": [{"text": "32%", "added": false}, {"text": "41%", "added": false}, {"text": "44%", "added": false}, {"text": "38%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The average of 15 results is 21. The average of the first 7 of those is 21 and the average of the last 7 is 20. What is the 8th result?", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2020", "added": false}, {"text": "2018", "added": false}, {"text": "2019", "added": false}, {"text": "2021", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "38", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2 cosec A", "added": false}, {"text": "2 cos A", "added": false}, {"text": "2 sec A", "added": false}, {"text": "2 sin A", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "The highest common factor of 108, 72 and 5a is a. What can be the least common multiple of 108, 72 and a?", "options": [{"text": "432", "added": false}, {"text": "324", "added": false}, {"text": "108", "added": false}, {"text": "216", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If the number 6336633P is divisible by 132, then the value of P is:", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The area of a circle is 1386 cm2. What is the radius of the circle? [Use π= 22/7]", "options": [{"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "21 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The price of one shirt is ₹700 in a shop, on which 10% discount is available for all customers. An additional 20% discount is there for the customers who pay in cash. What is the amount a customer has to pay for a shirt if he pays in cash?", "options": [{"text": "₹432", "added": false}, {"text": "₹504", "added": false}, {"text": "₹523", "added": false}, {"text": "₹514", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "The speeds of two bodies are in the ratio 2 : 3. If the difference in the time taken to cover 50 m is 10 sec, then find the difference in their speeds.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "If X, Y, Z and W are in fourth proportion. X = 3, Y = 13 and W = 39, determine Z.", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "537 : 389", "added": false}, {"text": "163 : 179", "added": false}, {"text": "179 : 163", "added": false}, {"text": "389 : 537", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The price of an article is first increased by 25% and later on, the price was decreased by 30% due to a reduction in sales. Find the net percentage change in the final price of the article.", "options": [{"text": "11.5% increased", "added": false}, {"text": "14% decreased", "added": false}, {"text": "13% increased", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5% decreased", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The production of AB Co. increased by 10% after one year, and in the next year it increased by 22%. In the third year, it increased by 5%. What overall change (in %) has been there in the production in three years from the original production?", "options": [{"text": "41.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "40.9%", "added": false}, {"text": "41.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "42.8%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "A", "added": false}, {"text": "C", "added": false}, {"text": "B", "added": false}, {"text": "E", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2019", "added": false}, {"text": "2018", "added": false}, {"text": "2016", "added": false}, {"text": "2017", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If the value of cosecA + cotA = m, then the value of cosecA – cotA is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "There are 3 taps, A, B and C, in a tank. These can fill the tank in 10 h, 20 h and 25 h, respectively. At first, all three taps are opened simultaneously. After 2 h, tap C is closed and tap A and B keep running. After 4 h, tap B is also closed. The remaining tank is filled by tap A alone. Find the percentage of work done by tap A itself.", "options": [{"text": "75%", "added": false}, {"text": "52%", "added": false}, {"text": "72%", "added": false}, {"text": "32%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "fill-empty", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A man goes 24 m towards east and then 10 m towards north. How far is he away from his initial position?", "options": [{"text": "23 m", "added": false}, {"text": "25 m", "added": false}, {"text": "26 m", "added": false}, {"text": "24 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A chord of a circle is equal to its radius of length 9 cm. Find the angle subtended by it in major segment.", "options": [{"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}, {"text": "120°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Find the amount if a sum of Rs.7,500 is invested on compound interest at 8% p.a. for 1.5 years when the interest is compounded half yearly.", "options": [{"text": "Rs.8,436.48", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.8,736.48", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.8,657.48", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.8,564.48", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "If a2 + b2 + 1 = 2a, then the value of a4 + b7 is:", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "A supermarket earns 5½% as discount on the total purchasing value and a bonus of ½% on sales more than Rs.10,000. What is the total sale value if it earns Rs.1,990?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.14,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.16,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.34,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.24,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "Chemistry", "added": false}, {"text": "Geography", "added": false}, {"text": "History", "added": false}, {"text": "CS", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "What is the radius of a normal cylinder whose height is 21 cm and curved surface area is 1386 cm2?", "options": [{"text": "10.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "10 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "Solve the following equation. (73 - 72 + 6) × (63 - 23 - 32 + 1) ÷ (212 + 202 - 41) = ___________.", "options": [{"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "What is the greatest positive integer that divides 554, 714 and 213 leaving the remainder 43, 57 and 67, respectively?", "options": [{"text": "95", "added": false}, {"text": "71", "added": false}, {"text": "83", "added": false}, {"text": "73", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Find the LCM of 25, 30, 50 and 75.", "options": [{"text": "15.0", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "1.50", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "If Cos θ + Sin θ = √2 Cos θ, find the value of (cos θ - Sinθ).", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "60 men can complete a work in 40 days. They start work together but after every 10 day, 5 men leave the work. In how many days will the work be completed?", "options": [{"text": "47.5", "added": false}, {"text": "49.5", "added": false}, {"text": "42.5", "added": false}, {"text": "45.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "If the number 8764x5 is divisible by 9, then find the least possible value of x where x is a two–digit number.", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "06", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "Find the HCF of 364 and 724.", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "364", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "Ajay buys 18 oranges for ₹90 and sells 15 oranges for ₹105. Find the percentage of his gain.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "The monthly incomes of Ravi and Shiv are in the ratio 1 : 2 and their monthly expenditures are in the ratio 1 : 3. If each saves ₹4,000 per month, then find the monthly income of Shiv.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "The length of a cold storage is 5 times its breadth, and its height is 8 m. The area of its four walls (including the doors) is 720 m2. Find the total surface area of cold storage.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "A truck goes from Haryana to Bangalore with an average speed of 60 km/h. The journey takes 30 hours. It returns from Bangalore to Haryana on the same road with an average speed of 40 km/h. What was the average speed of the truck during the roundtrip?", "options": [{"text": "60 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "40 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "50 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "48 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "In a journey of three unequal laps, a car covers a distance of 200 km in 4 h in the first lap, while another 162 km at the speed of 15 m/s in the second lap. It covered the remaining distance of the final lap in 4 h such that the average speed of the car for entire journey was 50 km/h. What was the speed of the car in the third lap of the journey?", "options": [{"text": "47 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "52 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "42 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "45 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "Three persons P, Q, R run along a circular track at speeds of 3 km/h, 4 km/h, 6 km/h, respectively. If the length of the track is 36 km, then after how much time will they meet again at the starting point?", "options": [{"text": "38 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "36 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "24 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "28 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "circular-track", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "A tangent is drawn from an external point ‘A’ to a circle of radius 12 cm. If the length of the tangent is 5 cm, then the distance from the centre of the circle to point ‘A’ is:", "options": [{"text": "17 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "13 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "The price of a bat and a ball are in the ratio 9 : 5. The price of the bat is Rs.380 more than the price of the ball. Find the price of the ball.", "options": [{"text": "Rs.470", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.485", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.475", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.480", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "The greatest number of five digits which is divisible by 13, 15, 18 and 21 is:", "options": [{"text": "99120", "added": false}, {"text": "98280", "added": false}, {"text": "96840", "added": false}, {"text": "95830", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "443", "added": false}, {"text": "256", "added": false}, {"text": "356", "added": false}, {"text": "401", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "Three metallic spheres of radii 10 cm, 8 cm and 6 cm, respectively, are melted to form a single solid cone of radius 12 cm. Find the curved surface area of the cone, correct to two places of decimal. (Take π = 3.14)", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "65.89%", "added": false}, {"text": "72.87%", "added": false}, {"text": "70.89%", "added": false}, {"text": "74.36%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}]}